From: UPF maintainers <upf@omecproject.org>
Subject: [PATCH] stl: calculate packet offsets without Scapy private state

The historical Stratum TRex fork relies on Scapy's private `_offset` field
when compiling named packet-field VM instructions.  That field is not
available with the caller-provided Scapy 2.7.0 distribution.  Calculate layer
and field offsets from serialized packet data instead, preserving named-field
VM support without depending on Scapy internals.

---
 scripts/automation/trex_control_plane/interactive/trex/stl/trex_stl_packet_builder_scapy.py | 51 +++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/automation/trex_control_plane/interactive/trex/stl/trex_stl_packet_builder_scapy.py b/scripts/automation/trex_control_plane/interactive/trex/stl/trex_stl_packet_builder_scapy.py
